From c21f19759a23c903e1c1d991d079862dd3885891 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 19 Aug 2026 13:09:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Add Halo volume generation performance benchmark harness

Adds performance_benchmark.py, which measures the cost of generating
spatial-reservation (Halo) clearance volumes over real IFC models at
increasing element counts, so the "thousands of Halo volumes" claim can be
evidenced rather than asserted.

- Halo generator producing watertight cylinder / sphere / rounded-box
  volumes at LOD 200/300/400, with the box case built as an exact Minkowski
  offset rather than a naively enlarged box.
- --validate mode checks every primitive for watertightness and verifies box
  volumes against the analytic Steiner-formula ground truth.
- Scenarios: 100/500/1000 elements single-model, 2000 elements federated
  across four IFC files with cross-model interference, an LOD sweep, and
  synthetic scale-out to 20000 volumes.
- Stages (parse / triangulate / Halo generation / interference detection)
  are timed independently so the bottleneck can be attributed.
- Emits JSON, CSV, Markdown tables and seven charts to docs/benchmarks/.
- Adds a bench uv dependency group (matplotlib, psutil).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01LF5NHxVz8VcTaVxmLcUykW
